      "title": "Confirm you recognize the administrator account <computer>\\<account-2>",
      "finding_ids": [
        "ACCT-EXTRA-ADMIN:fde0b291"
      ],
      "explanation": "The scan found a local user account, <computer>\\<account-2>, that has administrator rights. Administrator accounts can change anything on the computer, so it's worth knowing about each one. Having a separate administrator account is actually good practice, and many households have one on purpose, so this is often completely normal. It only becomes a concern if you don't recognize the account, because an unknown administrator account can be a sign that someone else got in. This was the first scan, so there was no earlier scan to show whether the account was added recently. If you recognize it, you can leave it as it is. If you don't, look at the fix shown for this finding in the report."
